# The fork of Idris's compiler (compiler/idris) carries the change of
# upstream/52-relevant-implicit-split/pull-request.diff: a case tree splits
# an argument the clauses leave to unification after the patterns that fix
# it, in the coverage check's tree at every quantity. Main.idr's `fp4`,
# `sumF`, the case block of `cb` and the with block of `wb`, which run and
# leave the relevant index `ws` to unification, are covering under
# `%default total`; the pinned, unpatched Idris reports each not covering,
# with two missing cases, and refuses the module. `liftedBad` has an
# argument whose type computes on the index, which the tree must split
# first. When a re-sync brings upstream's fix, the report, its PINS.md entry
# and this test go (upstream/README.md).
. "$IDRIS_MLIR_ROOT/tests/testutils.sh"
profile_accept .
